CORE gcc-only
main.c

^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
^PARSING ERROR$
--
Tests that __builtin_has_attribute(expr, attr) parses (both the bare-name
and name-with-arguments forms) and is modelled as a compile-time constant
(false) -- the _Static_assert mirrors the Linux fortify-string strscpy
pattern and only compiles if the builtin folds to a constant.
